---
import { Body } from 'govuk-react/body';
import * as Details from 'govuk-react/details';
import { GridColumn } from 'govuk-react/grid-column';
import { GridRow } from 'govuk-react/grid-row';
import { Heading } from 'govuk-react/heading';
import { FeedbackField, GuideAccordion } from '../features/islands';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Islands">
  <GridRow>
    <GridColumn width="two-thirds">
      <Heading size="l" headingLevel={1}>Islands</Heading>
      <Body>
        Astro renders every component on this page to HTML. Only the components with a client directive hydrate in the
        browser, each as its own island, so React only runs where it’s needed.
      </Body>

      <Heading size="m" headingLevel={2}>Without a directive</Heading>
      <Body>This details component has no directive, so it sends no JavaScript. It works as HTML.</Body>
      <Details.Composite summary="Help with nationality">
        We need to know your nationality so we can work out which elections you’re entitled to vote in.
      </Details.Composite>

      <Heading size="m" headingLevel={2}>When the browser is idle</Heading>
      <Body>This character count has <code>client:idle</code>. It hydrates once the page has loaded and the browser is idle.</Body>
      <FeedbackField client:idle />

      <Heading size="m" headingLevel={2}>When it’s visible</Heading>
      <Body>
        This accordion has <code>client:visible</code>. It hydrates when it scrolls into view. Until then, it shows every section, as it does without
        JavaScript.
      </Body>
      <GuideAccordion client:visible id="islands-guide" />
    </GridColumn>
  </GridRow>
</Layout>
